Ladybird’s table fixup now wraps an absolutely positioned row group,
row or caption in an anonymous row and cell, which gives it its static
position among the rows. Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5 give
the same box position and table height in all eight cases of the new
test, run with engine-compare, including the extra border spacing the
anonymous row adds and a row group placed before its thead.

Blink’s LayoutTable::CanBeDirectChild() accepts only captions, columns
and sections, so LayoutBlock::AddChild() puts a blockified row group in
an anonymous section (CreateAnonymousChild()). In WebKit, a RenderTable
keeps only captions, sections and column groups as direct children, and
RenderTreeBuilder::Table::findOrCreateParentForChild() wraps the rest in
an anonymous RenderTableSection. And in Gecko, nsCSSFrameConstructor::
CreateNeededPseudoContainers() builds the anonymous table parts. All of
this paragraph comes from reading their sources, not from running them.
